 "unresolved_reasons": {
  "ANZ_WPLauncher": "the round is the Hydra 70 white-phosphorus warhead (M156 and M259, both published), but the identity carries no designation of it. The only token that would reach the Hydra 70 row is the two-letter 'WP', and as a curated alias it would also capture every unrelated white-phosphorus round in the content (rhs_ammo_152_WP, rhs_mag_WP_2a33, vn_sh_76mm_wp, cup_sh_105_wp and others), so the corpus declines it.",
  "DSA_MachinePistol45": "the identity names a chambering and a category ('.45 Machine-pistol'), never a published weapon designation, and the small-arms corpus holds real weapons only: neither the classname nor the display names one.",
  "DSA_MachinePistol9mm": "the identity names a chambering and a category ('9mm Machine-pistol'), never a published weapon designation, and the small-arms corpus holds real weapons only: neither the classname nor the display names one.",
  "FIR_Smokewinder": "it is not a munition. It is a smoke-generating display pod (SmokeWinder) that mounts on a Sidewinder rail, so it is equipment, and its identity carries no kind phrase: the kind filter names kinds, and 'Smokewinder' is the product's own name, so neither the corpus nor the filter may key on it.",
  "PHEN_FSPLUS_AsphyxiantBomb_Unguided_rack": "the identity names a chemical filling and a mod tier ('[Tier 2] Asphyxiant Gas'), never a published munition designation. No published munition pairs a Mk 82 body with an asphyxiant agent, so naming it would invent the item.",
  "PHEN_FSPLUS_BlisterBomb_Unguided_rack": "the identity names a chemical filling ('Blister Agent'), never a published munition designation. No published munition pairs a Mk 82 body with a blister agent, so naming it would invent the item.",
  "PHEN_FSPLUS_NerveBomb_Unguided_rack": "the identity names a chemical filling and a mod tier ('[Tier 3] Nerve Gas'), never a published munition designation. No published munition pairs a Mk 82 body with a nerve agent, so naming it would invent the item.",
  "PHEN_FSPLUS_NovaBomb_Unguided_rack": "the identity names a fictional agent and a mod tier ('[Tier 5] Nova Gas'), never a published munition designation. 'Nova gas' has no real-world counterpart, so naming it would invent the item.",
  "PHEN_FSPLUS_RiotCSGasBomb_Unguided_rack": "the identity names a riot-control agent and a mod tier ('[Tier 1] Riot CS Gas'), never a published munition designation. The published CS munitions are grenades and projectors, not a Mk 82-bodied aircraft bomb, so naming it would pair two things no source pairs.",
  "disco_nimrod_bomb_launcher": "the identity names a nominal weight and a category ('1000 lb HE bombs'), never a published designation. The store it drops is the British 1,000 lb General-Purpose bomb, which the corpus now holds, but reaching it would need the bare weight '1000lb' to be a designation, and that is exactly what identity_designations refuses: it would also capture every other 1,000 lb-class store (rksla3_wpn_uk_pw2_1000 among them) and resolve them to a bomb they do not name.",
  "rhs_weap_M301": "the cannon is the XM301, published under that designation only. The classname and the display both drop the X, and no source the corpus holds publishes 'M301', so a sourced alias cannot bridge the two.",
  "rksla3_wpn_ba21": "no source the corpus holds publishes a 'BA-21' munition. The English Wikipedia title BA-21 is a Soviet armoured car, and the Chinese Blue Arrow 21 has no article in either the English or the Chinese edition.",
  "rksla3_wpn_fulger_sam": "no source the corpus holds publishes this designation. The mod's own magazine text ('MDBA Fulger') names no maker or document, and no encyclopaedia article exists for a missile of that name.",
  "rksla3_wpn_furypgm": "no source the corpus holds publishes this designation. 'FURY PGM' appears only in the mod, and its ammunition derives from the GBU-12, which is a different munition.",
  "rksla3_wpn_gp19_pod": "the pod carries the GAU-19 .50 cal gun, which the corpus holds, but neither the classname nor the display carries the gun's designation: 'GP19' is the pod's own label and no source the corpus holds publishes it.",
  "rksla3_wpn_mikholit": "no source the corpus holds publishes this designation. The mod defines a four-round box of 10 kg guided submunitions under a name that appears nowhere else.",
  "rksla3_wpn_sampt21": "no source the corpus holds publishes this designation. The mod labels a 400 kg general-purpose bomb 'SAMPT21 GP'; SAMP/T is a different weapon (a surface-to-air system), and the mod's own ammunition derives from the Mk 82."
 }
}
